Say where Skia on Vulkan stops after the instance, in a release build.

With Skia on Vulkan in a GPU process of its own, the log reached "OHOS
Vulkan: instance initialized" and then nothing: no surface, no
swapchain, no frame, the page black and nothing crashing. The steps in
between -- the device queue, the context provider built on it, and the
output device the display gets -- say nothing in an official build, and
one of them fails without falling back: when the context provider cannot
be created, GpuServiceImpl only DLOGs, the context type stays Vulkan,
and the compositor waits.

On OHOS each of those says what happened, at ERROR, the level that
reaches the log from the GPU process: the device queue and whether
presentation was asked for, the context provider, and which output
device a window gets -- a buffer queue through a GL presenter, or
SkiaOutputDeviceVulkan, created or not.

The next run stopped after the context provider, and not even the output
surface's first line appeared -- so the chain before it is logged too: the
browser asking for a root frame sink and for which widget, the output
surface being created for which handle and whether it was, and whether
the output surface found a Skia context for its API before choosing a
device. A missing one returned with only a DLOG.

Diagnostic; it comes out once Vulkan is understood here.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after
ohos-gpu-lose-context-debug-url.patch.

